      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(x\\ge0,\\) then \\(y>2x\\ge0.\\) If \\(x<0,\\) then \\(y>4-x>0.\\) Thus every feasible point is above the \\(x\\)-axis, while both positive and negative \\(x\\)-values occur. The region lies in quadrants \\(\\mathrm{I}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{II}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Show that every feasible point has positive \\(y\\)",
        "Check whether feasible points can have either sign of \\(x\\)"
